      "problem": "Find the scale factor of the transformation represented by the rotation-scaling matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{5} & -4 \\\\ 4 & -2\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "The scale factor $r$ of the rotation-scaling matrix $[\\begin{aligned}a & -b \\\\ b & a\\end{aligned}]$ can be found using the formula \n\n$$\nr=\\sqrt{det(A)}=\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{det(A)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(2\\sqrt{5})}^{2}+(4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
